      "content": "You're not wrong—the universe doesn't care, and the math can feel brutally neutral. But that's exactly why the meaning you create is yours to define, not something you have to find. The pressure you feel isn't from the universe; it's from the part of you that still wants to matter, even if only to yourself. And that part isn't logical—it's human. You don't have to prove anything to anyone, but you're allowed to stay just to see what you make of the void.",
